%[text] # ADS-B Prediction Pipeline Stage Review
%[text] This Live Script is the single Run All review entry point for the ADS-B prediction-step experiment. It connects the early smoke results to the frozen Expanded-3Day partitions, a held-out test comparison of native and neural models, a neural validation-versus-test comparison, and three configurable one-step trajectory collections. No model is trained, clipped, smoothed, or promoted here.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text]
%#ok<*NOPTS>
stageReviewScriptPath = string(which("stageReviewLiveScript"));
projectRoot = string(fileparts(stageReviewScriptPath));
addpath(projectRoot);
if ~exist("enableInteractiveGlobe", "var")
    enableInteractiveGlobe = true;
end
if ~exist("stage4CGlobeTrajectoryCount", "var")
    stage4CGlobeTrajectoryCount = 50;
end
review = helperBuildStageReviewArtifacts("ProjectRoot", projectRoot);
stage4CDashboard = helperBuildStage4CReviewDashboard( ...
    "ProjectRoot", projectRoot);
trainingDetails = helperBuildStageReviewTrainingDetails(review);
trackDiagnostics = helperBuildStageReviewTrackDiagnostics(review);
selectedTrackHex = trackDiagnostics.easyTrackHex;
turnDiagnosticTrackHex = trackDiagnostics.turnDiagnosticTrackHex;
mlpDiagnostics = helperBuildStageReviewMLPDiagnostics( ...
    review, ...
    "TrackHex", selectedTrackHex);
phaseSummary = review.phaseSummaryTable %[output:9ed9975e]
metricComparison = review.metricComparisonTable %[output:5a719b13]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 2B Data And Smoke Training
%[text] Stage 2B converted local ADS-B truth into adjacent state pairs in Sensor Fusion order |\[x, vx, y, vy, z, vz\]|. It also trained a small MLP in MATLAB. This was a software plumbing check: the split, normalization, network output shape, loss, and positive variance transform were tested, but the model is not a useful predictor.
stage2BDatasetSummary = table( ...
    ["usable pairs"; "aircraft tracks"; "median dt [s]"; ...
    "constvel position RMSE [m]"; "smoke MLP position RMSE [m]"], ...
    [ ...
        review.dataset.buildSummary.usablePairCount; ...
        review.characterization.diversityAssessment.aircraftCount; ...
        review.dataset.buildSummary.dtSummary.median; ...
        review.dataset.baselineConstVelMetrics.positionRMSEMeters; ...
        review.trainingSummary.modelPositionRMSEMeters], ...
    'VariableNames', ["metric", "value"])
%%
%[text] ## NN Training Details
%[text] The training code is |trainLocalADSBMLPSmoke.m|. The saved artifact is loaded from |artifacts/stage2B/localADSBMLPSmokeTraining.mat|. There is no classification accuracy because this is regression; the end-of-run quality indicators are loss, RMSE, and empirical covariance coverage. The validation split exists, but this smoke run did not use it for early stopping or model selection.
trainingScriptPath = fullfile(projectRoot, ...
    "trainLocalADSBMLPSmoke.m")
trainingDetails
%%
%[text] ## Why The Smoke MLP Line Goes The Wrong Way
%[text] The Stage 2B smoke MLP line is the actual saved output, not a plotting artifact. On the easy track below, |constvel| is within meters while the smoke MLP predicts points tens of kilometers away. The model only ran a tiny smoke-training pass, and its normalized outputs collapsed toward a low-spread dataset-level prior instead of learning one-step aircraft motion.
mlpDiagnosis = mlpDiagnostics.diagnosisText
selectedTrackSplitSummary = mlpDiagnostics.splitSummary
mlpExamplePredictions = mlpDiagnostics.examplePredictionTable
mlpNormalizedSpread = mlpDiagnostics.normalizedSpreadTable
mlpLossHistory = mlpDiagnostics.lossHistoryTable
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3A Delta-Target MLP
%[text] Stage 3A trains the MLP on state deltas and reconstructs the next state as |previousState + predictedDelta|. The neural input stays motion-focused: velocity, local altitude, elapsed time, covariance diagonal for interface compatibility, and physics-derived delta features. Absolute horizontal |x| and |y| are not default neural features.
if review.hasStage3A
    stage3TrainingScriptPath = fullfile( ...
        projectRoot, ...
        "trainLocalADSBMLPStage3.m")
    stage3TrainingReportPath = fullfile( ...
        projectRoot, ...
        "artifacts", ...
        "stage3", ...
        "stage3LocalADSBMLPTrainingReport.md")
    stage3MetricComparison = review.metricComparisonTable
    stage3HeadlineRMSE = review.metricComparisonTable( ...
        ismember( ...
        review.metricComparisonTable.method, ...
        ["constvel baseline", "Stage 3A delta MLP"]), ...
        ["method", "positionRMSEMeters", ...
        "velocityRMSEMetersPerSecond"])
    stage3TrainingLadder = ...
        review.stage3Summary.trainingLadder.ladderTable
    stage3FeatureAblation = ...
        review.stage3Summary.trainingLadder.featureAblationTable
    stage3ManeuverMetrics = ...
        review.stage3Summary.metrics.byManeuverClass
else
    stage3Status = ...
        "No Stage 3A training artifact found. Run trainLocalADSBMLPStage3.m to populate this section."
end
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3A Constvel Versus Delta MLP Error
%[text] This plot focuses on native |constvel| and the Stage 3A delta-target MLP for the selected review track. The top panel is row-wise one-step 3-D position error. The lower panel is cumulative position RMSE through each timestep.
if review.hasStage3A
    stage3TrackErrorComparison = ...
        helperPlotStageReviewStage3ErrorComparison( ...
        review, ...
        "TrackHex", selectedTrackHex, ...
        "MaxPairs", 80)
else
    stage3TrackErrorComparison = table( ...
        "Stage 3A artifact missing", ...
        NaN, ...
        NaN, ...
        NaN, ...
        'VariableNames', [ ...
            "method", ...
            "trackPositionRMSEMeters", ...
            "trackMedianPositionErrorMeters", ...
            "trackP95PositionErrorMeters"])
end
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3B Aggregate ADS-B Evaluation
%[text] Stage 3B freezes the Stage 3A network and compares it with native |constvel| on every eligible local ADS-B state pair that can be aggregated from the capture tree. This is an evidence and data-readiness gate, not a retraining run.
if review.hasStage3B
    stage3BEvaluationScriptPath = fullfile( ...
        projectRoot, ...
        "runStage3BAggregateADSBEvaluation.m")
    stage3BEvaluationReportPath = review.stage3BSummary.reportPath
    stage3BAggregateRMSE = review.stage3BMetricComparisonTable
    stage3BRecommendation = ...
        review.stage3BDataReadiness.recommendation
    stage3BDataReadiness = ...
        review.stage3BDataReadiness.gateTable
    stage3BSourceInventory = review.stage3BSummary.inventoryTable
    stage3BFigurePaths = struct2table( ...
        review.stage3BSummary.figurePaths, ...
        "AsArray", true)
else
    stage3BStatus = ...
        "No Stage 3B aggregate evaluation artifact found. Run runStage3BAggregateADSBEvaluation.m to populate this section."
end
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3B Position Absolute Error Separation
%[text] This figure plots every Stage 3B one-step position absolute error on one set of axes. Blue points are native |constvel| and red points are the frozen Stage 3A MLP, matching the Stage 3A target-comparison color convention.
if review.hasStage3B
    stage3BPositionAbsErrorSummary = ...
        helperPlotStage3BPositionAbsError(review.stage3BSummary)
else
    stage3BPositionAbsErrorStatus = ...
        "No Stage 3B aggregate evaluation artifact found. Run runStage3BAggregateADSBEvaluation.m before plotting position absolute error."
end
%%
%[text] ## Stage 3B Track-Level Diagnostics
%[text] These rows help identify whether the frozen Stage 3A MLP is consistently worse than |constvel| or whether the error is concentrated in specific aircraft tracks or update regimes.
if review.hasStage3B
    stage3BTopTracks = review.stage3BTrackSummary( ...
        1:min(8, height(review.stage3BTrackSummary)), :)
    stage3BManeuverMetrics = ...
        review.stage3BSummary.metrics.byManeuverClass
    stage3BDtRegimeMetrics = ...
        review.stage3BSummary.metrics.byDtRegime
else
    stage3BTopTracks = table( ...
        "Stage 3B artifact missing", ...
        NaN, ...
        'VariableNames', ["status", "value"])
end
%%
%[text] ## Frozen Expanded-3Day Partitions
%[text] The Stage 4C review now uses the frozen global ICAO-disjoint split. The first table shows train, validation, and test allocation. The cross-tabulation then shows how every one of the 457,903 state pairs is distributed across the four retrospective motion classes.
expandedSplitAllocation = stage4CDashboard.splitSummaryTable %[output:783a7dd1]
expandedMotionClassAllocation = ... %[output:group:9fa231ca] %[output:457bf4ca]
    stage4CDashboard.motionClassSplitTable %[output:group:9fa231ca] %[output:457bf4ca]
stage4CModelIdentities = stage4CDashboard.modelIdentityTable %[output:3d86aeef]
%%
%[text] ## Held-Out Test Comparison: Native Models And Frozen NNs
%[text] This primary dashboard uses held-out test rows only. The native |constvel|, |constacc|, and |constturn| algorithms are deterministic and are not trained or validated; “test” identifies only the frozen data rows used for this fair comparison. Each dashboard row compares the class-aligned native model with the same three frozen neural networks using pair-weighted aggregate 3-D errors on matched rows.
stage4CTestRMSEFigure = helperPlotStage4CRMSEDashboard( ... %[output:group:3c31aa5b] %[output:65e2774a] %[output:5c7b81aa]
    stage4CDashboard.rmseTable) %[output:group:3c31aa5b] %[output:65e2774a] %[output:5c7b81aa]
stage4CTestRMSEComparison = stage4CTestRMSEFigure.metricTable %[output:8d774de9]
%%
%[text] ## Neural Validation Versus Test
%[text] This secondary dashboard excludes the native algorithms and compares validation with test performance for the three frozen neural networks. The split labels describe two held-out data partitions; no network is trained or updated in this Live Script. Similar validation and test errors support stability across the partitions, while a large gap can indicate model-selection bias or partition shift.
stage4CNNGeneralizationFigure = ... %[output:group:0ba4dc7e] %[output:90630829] %[output:91890529]
    helperPlotStage4CNNValidationTest(stage4CDashboard.rmseTable) %[output:group:0ba4dc7e] %[output:90630829] %[output:91890529]
stage4CNNGeneralizationComparison = ... %[output:group:3cc8b830] %[output:4b0869ed]
    stage4CNNGeneralizationFigure.metricTable %[output:group:3cc8b830] %[output:4b0869ed]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 4C Native Maneuver Baselines
%[text] Stage 4C keeps the trained networks frozen and asks a narrower physics question. On retrospectively labeled |constacc\_like| rows, native |constacc| receives raw three-dimensional acceleration from the immediately preceding observation. On |constturn\_like| rows, native |constturn| receives a wrapped raw heading-rate estimate. The current target and maneuver label do not enter prediction, and ICAO is used only to find the predecessor and preserve the frozen split.
stage4CNativeEvaluationScriptPath = fullfile( ... %[output:group:71861aa7] %[output:640a47fc]
    projectRoot, ... %[output:640a47fc]
    "runStage4CNativeManeuverBaselineEvaluation.m") %[output:group:71861aa7] %[output:640a47fc]
stage4CNativeCoverage = ... %[output:group:0bcbc034] %[output:4bae20c2]
    review.stage4CNativeManeuverBaseline.coverageTable %[output:group:0bcbc034] %[output:4bae20c2]
stage4CNativeInitializationDiagnostics = ... %[output:group:9b8f1b65] %[output:7a78efdc]
    review.stage4CNativeManeuverBaseline.initializationDiagnostics %[output:group:9b8f1b65] %[output:7a78efdc]
stage4CNativeMetrics = review.stage4CNativeMetricTable %[output:349b0d53]
stage4CNativeFigurePath = ... %[output:group:646d700d] %[output:964f48c4]
    review.stage4CNativeManeuverBaseline.figurePath %[output:group:646d700d] %[output:964f48c4]
%%
%[text] ## Why Raw Causal Initialization Can Spike
%[text] Finite differences turn small velocity or timing changes into acceleration and turn-rate estimates. Short intervals and quantized ADS-B velocity can therefore create large raw values, especially turn-rate spikes. Stage 4C deliberately leaves every finite estimate unclipped and unsmoothed so this first baseline exposes that sensitivity. Bounded or smoothed causal initialization remains a deferred sensitivity study.
stage4CNativeSensitivityStudy = ... %[output:group:4104a8fb] %[output:44b9bccd]
    review.stage4CNativeManeuverBaseline.deferredSensitivityStudy %[output:group:4104a8fb] %[output:44b9bccd]
%%
%[text] ## Raw ADS-B Tracks In Local Coordinates
%[text] These are ADS-B-derived next-state positions in the local east-north-up frame. The historical plot provides context for the much larger Expanded-3Day dashboard that follows.
helperPlotStageReviewLocalTracks(review, "MaxTracks", 8); %[output:6f6a9a58]
%%
%[text] ## What The Motion Labels Mean
%[text] The labels are not network outputs or model-selection inputs. They are offline diagnostic labels computed from each observed ADS-B state pair: heading change comes from velocity direction, speed change comes from horizontal speed magnitude, vertical-rate change comes from |vz|, and sparse update comes from |dtSeconds|.
labelRules = review.labelRuleSummaryTable %[output:64123ae1]
maneuverCounts = review.maneuverCountsTable %[output:37093ca4]
%%
%[text] ## Historical Maneuver Coverage And Baseline Error
%[text] The Stage 2B artifact was dominated by |constvel\_like| behavior. This historical view explains why the project collected Expanded-3Day data before the Stage 4C comparisons.
helperPlotStageReviewManeuverSummary(review); %[output:8c9b3c25]
%%
%[text] ## Historical Track Selection For Review
%[text] The earlier easy review track is selected from tracks with at least 40 pairs and at least 70 percent |constvel\_like| labels, then sorted by lowest median |constvel| position error. It remains here to connect the original smoke workflow to Stage 4C.
trackSelectionNote = trackDiagnostics.selectionNote
selectedTrackHex
turnDiagnosticTrackHex
topTrackDiagnostics = trackDiagnostics.trackTable( ...
    1:min(8, height(trackDiagnostics.trackTable)), :)
%%
%[text] ## One Historical Track: Truth, Constvel, Smoke NN, And Stage 3A
%[text] - Green is ADS-B-derived next-state truth
%[text] - Blue is native |constvel|, gray is the saved Stage 2B smoke MLP, and red is Stage 3A
%[text] - Gray smoke-MLP excursions are retained as a reminder that Stage 2B was only a plumbing check \
helperPlotStageReviewPredictionComparison( ...
    review, ...
    "TrackHex", selectedTrackHex, ...
    "MaxPairs", 80);
%%
%[text] ## Constvel-Like Trajectory Collection
%[text] Here |N| means the longest |N| continuous eligible test events in this motion class, using deterministic session, ICAO, time, and dataset-row tie-breakers. The default is |stage4CGlobeTrajectoryCount = 50|; change it to |100|, |500|, |1e3|, or another positive integer and rerun only this section. The helper caps |N| at availability and reports requested and plotted event counts, total pairs, sessions, ICAOs, and the resulting |5N| paths.
constvelRepresentative = stage4CDashboard.representatives(1);
constvelRepresentativeSummary = ... %[output:group:2259d9d7] %[output:04bffa33]
    constvelRepresentative.summaryTable %[output:group:2259d9d7] %[output:04bffa33]
constvelGlobeLegend = constvelRepresentative.legendTable %[output:9ead548d]
if enableInteractiveGlobe %[output:group:86ec248b]
    constvelGlobeOutput = ...
        helperOpenStage4CReviewGlobe( ...
        stage4CDashboard, ...
        "constvel_like", ...
        TrajectoryCount=stage4CGlobeTrajectoryCount);
    constvelViewer = constvelGlobeOutput.viewer;
    constvelTrajectoryCollectionSummary = ... %[output:61da1f9f]
        constvelGlobeOutput.collection.summaryTable %[output:61da1f9f]
    constvelGlobeLegend = constvelGlobeOutput.legendTable %[output:191522d0]
end %[output:group:86ec248b]
%%
%[text] ## Constacc-Like Trajectory Collection
%[text] This independent globe applies the same longest-first |N| rule to eligible |constacc\_like| events. It overlays ADS-B truth, native |constacc|, Stage 3A legacy, Expanded scratch, and Expanded warm one-step paths without clipping or smoothing.
constaccRepresentative = stage4CDashboard.representatives(2);
constaccRepresentativeSummary = ... %[output:group:6aec63dd] %[output:90360451]
    constaccRepresentative.summaryTable %[output:group:6aec63dd] %[output:90360451]
constaccGlobeLegend = constaccRepresentative.legendTable %[output:706d5adb]
if enableInteractiveGlobe %[output:group:5c51c5fa]
    constaccGlobeOutput = ...
        helperOpenStage4CReviewGlobe( ...
        stage4CDashboard, ...
        "constacc_like", ...
        TrajectoryCount=stage4CGlobeTrajectoryCount);
    constaccViewer = constaccGlobeOutput.viewer;
    constaccTrajectoryCollectionSummary = ... %[output:94c998b2]
        constaccGlobeOutput.collection.summaryTable %[output:94c998b2]
    constaccGlobeLegend = constaccGlobeOutput.legendTable %[output:7536cc2f]
end %[output:group:5c51c5fa]
%%
%[text] ## Constturn-Like Trajectory Collection
%[text] This independent globe applies the same longest-first |N| rule to eligible |constturn\_like| events. It overlays ADS-B truth, native |constturn|, Stage 3A legacy, Expanded scratch, and Expanded warm one-step paths while retaining the raw heading-rate initialization used by the frozen Stage 4C evaluation.
constturnRepresentative = stage4CDashboard.representatives(3);
constturnRepresentativeSummary = ... %[output:group:4d900a6a] %[output:89da537b]
    constturnRepresentative.summaryTable %[output:group:4d900a6a] %[output:89da537b]
constturnGlobeLegend = constturnRepresentative.legendTable %[output:8535bafa]
if enableInteractiveGlobe %[output:group:18b9a56b]
    constturnGlobeOutput = ...
        helperOpenStage4CReviewGlobe( ...
        stage4CDashboard, ...
        "constturn_like", ...
        TrajectoryCount=stage4CGlobeTrajectoryCount);
    constturnViewer = constturnGlobeOutput.viewer;
    constturnTrajectoryCollectionSummary = ... %[output:06282e32]
        constturnGlobeOutput.collection.summaryTable %[output:06282e32]
    constturnGlobeLegend = constturnGlobeOutput.legendTable %[output:54c61101]
end %[output:group:18b9a56b]
%%
%[text] ## Current Interpretation
%[text] The Expanded-3Day scratch and warm networks greatly improve on Stage 3A legacy but do not beat |constvel| position RMSE. Raw causal |constacc| and |constturn| expose useful model behavior on matched maneuver rows, including turn-rate sensitivity, but do not justify promotion. These are sequences of one-step predictions from observed states, not recursive forecasts or tracker outputs.
finalInterpretation = ...
    "Stage 4C remains evaluation-only; no learned or native model is promoted."

